NOTES:
- Microlensing simulation with pyLIMA for LSST
PARAMS:
  alpha: Binary lens trajectory angle (optional, radians)
  event_id: Event ID source file
  f_blend: Blending fraction
  m_g: Baseline magnitude in g band
  m_i: Baseline magnitude in i band
  m_r: Baseline magnitude in r band
  m_u: Baseline magnitude in u band
  m_y: Baseline magnitude in y band
  m_z: Baseline magnitude in z band
  model: Theorical model (e.g., USBL, FSPL, PSPL)
  piEE: Parallax component East (optional)
  piEN: Parallax component North (optional)
  q: Binary lens mass ratio (optional)
  rho: Source radius (optional, dimensionless)
  s: Binary lens separation (optional, dimensionless)
  system_type: Physical system type (e.g., single or binary lensing)
  t0: Time of peak magnification (days)
  tE: Einstein crossing time (days)
  u0: Impact parameter (dimensionless)
PURPOSE: Microlensing model based on synthetic datasets
